    "done_when": "A codex subscription can carry one banked reset. The lead wants to flag it once as available. While it is available, the budget group has one extra week of allowance on top of what remains in the current seven-day window. The extra allowance never stacks: flagging it again while it is already available changes nothing and says so. The lead marks it used, or reckon detects its use automatically.\n\n1. A durable per-budget-group flag under the crew state home, written atomically, with the time it was set and by whom. Expose it through reckon crew subcommands:\n   - reckon crew budget-reset --group codex-sub --available, idempotent: reports already-available without stacking;\n   - reckon crew budget-reset --group codex-sub --used;\n   - reckon crew budget-reset --group codex-sub, which prints the state.\n   Pick the subcommand name to match existing crew naming, and say what you chose.\n2. While the flag is available, the budget pace for that group counts one extra full window of allowance (one seven-day window, capped at +1). The burn multiple, pace allowance and projected exhaustion that budget preflight and the picker read reflect it, and the reading carries reset_available: true so Jev sees why. Change this in reckon/budget.py's pace computation, so preflight and the picker both get it.\n3. Detect use automatically where the readings allow it. A seven-day window whose resets_at jumps forward to about now plus the window length while the previously observed resets_at is still in the future (so utilisation fell before the scheduled reset) is a consumed reset. In that case clear the flag and record the event with both readings. Natural reset at the scheduled time must not clear the flag.\n4. Tests:\n   - the non-stacking idempotence;\n   - the pace with and without the flag, from the same reading;\n   - automatic use-detection, on a fixture pair of readings and on a natural reset that must not clear it;\n   - the CLI round trip on a temp RECKON_HOME.\n   No test writes outside its temp home.\n5. Evidence in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/codex-banked-reset.html.\n\nDo not edit reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py or reckon/crew/paid_lanes.py, which a concurrent node owns. If the reset_available field does not reach the picker candidate through the allowance mapping budget already returns, report that as a follow-on rather than editing those files.\n\nGate: tests/test_budget*.py, tests/test_picker_pressure.py, tests/test_burn_admission.py and the new test file tests/test_codex_banked_reset.py. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
